  "passage": "A university built a digital model of a city to test traffic plans. On the screen, cars, buses, bikes, and pedestrians moved through virtual streets.\nStudents watched engineers test what would happen if one road became bus-only. The model predicted less traffic in one area but more in another.\nThe engineer explained that a digital model is useful, but it is not the real city. People may behave differently from predictions.\nThe students learned that planning needs both simulation and observation.\nA digital twin can help people imagine consequences before building. But the real city still has weather, habits, emotions, and surprises.",
